y to make it at least 75% of  baseball writers had to vote for him for  several years Walker barely hit 20% in  2014 he felt it 10% but as the log jam  of superstars became enshrined in those  years walker's chances improved and with  modern analytics Walker's all-round game  looked better and better  he reached 34% and last year almost 55%  and in this his last year he would need  another big jump Walker needed 75% of  the votes cast his final total he  cleared 76 percent Larry Walker becomes  the first position player and second  canadian-born member  of the National Baseball Hall of Fame it  is one of the most stunning changes of  heart in the history of Hall of Fame  voting more than triple the support  Walker had three years ago from baseball  writers in his last swing for the Hall  of Fame Walker joins the likes of Jim  Rice and another Expo Tim Raines each  voted in in their last year of  eligibility to be enshrined in  baseball's Hall of Fame in his last  chance was like Larry Walker in the  bottom of the ninth one more time he  came through in the clutch  Eric Sorensen Global News Toronto well  done that is global national for this  Tuesday I'm Robin Gill  tonight your Canada is Canmore Alberta  we would love to see your corner of this  country so email your pictures to  viewers at global national calm thank  you for watching and have a great night  [Music]
 

